-- PM: SLEEPCFG and STDBYCFG
+- PM: SLEEPCFG and STDBYCFG. A WFI with SLEEPCFG = STANDBY stops every
+  GCLK peripheral channel that no enabled peripheral with RUNSTDBY asks
+  for, and the CPU clock with SysTick, as a PIC32CM MC00 does (a channel
+  is gated, so everything on a running channel counts; sources and
+  generators run on demand); what still runs wakes the core. The SoC's
+  ``standby`` property does the same without a WFI.
